---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Live memory demo"
  description="Write up to 100,000 synthetic agent memories to the real instantKV Rust engine. Recall exact records in a separate reader and inspect measured latency."
>
  <main id="main" class="container demo-page" data-pagefind-body>
    <section class="demo-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Live storage / real Rust engine</span>
        <h1>
          100,000 memories.
          <br />
          <span class="chrome-text">One exact recall.</span>
        </h1>
        <p>
          Write a fleet's worth of agent context. Clear the writer. Retrieve any
          record from the reader—with timings from the actual requests.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="demo-live">
        <span class="signal"></span> CLOUDFLARE EDGE → INSTANTKV
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="demo-toolbar">
      <label>
        Storage mode
        <select id="storage-mode">
          <option value="cache">RAM cache · 15-minute TTL</option>
          <option value="durable">Durable redb · 15-minute TTL</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label>
        Memories
        <select id="memory-count">
          <option value="1000">1,000</option>
          <option value="10000" selected>
            10,000
          </option>
          <option value="50000">50,000</option>
          <option value="100000">100,000</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label>
        Context length
        <select id="value-size">
          <option value="256">256 characters</option>
          <option value="512" selected>
            512 characters
          </option>
          <option value="1024">1,024 characters</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <span class="demo-limit">
        64 synthetic agents
        <br />
        16 concurrent backend requests
      </span>
    </div>

    <section class="demo-panels" aria-label="Independent writer and reader">
      <article class="demo-panel">
        <div class="demo-panel-heading">
          <span class="eyebrow">01 / Writer</span>
          <span class="demo-terminal-label">PUT → STORAGE</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Give the fleet a memory.</h2>
        <label for="memory-content">Context to store in each record</label>
        <textarea
          id="memory-content"
          rows="3"
          maxlength="128"
        >Use Rust + redb. Shared knowledge is read-only for workers. Keep source references with every decision.</textarea>
        <div class="demo-actions">
          <button id="start-run" class="button button-primary" type="button">
            Store 10,000 memories →
          </button>
          <button id="stop-run" class="button" type="button" disabled>
            Pause
          </button>
          <button id="new-run" class="button" type="button">
            New run
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="demo-progress-label">
          <span id="write-count">0 / 10,000 acknowledged</span>
          <span id="write-percent">0%</span>
        </div>
        <progress
          id="write-progress"
          value="0"
          max="10000"
          aria-label="Acknowledged writes"
        ></progress>
        <div class="memory-grid" id="memory-grid" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <p class="demo-caption">
          Each illuminated cell represents acknowledged records.
        </p>
        <div class="demo-panel-heading">
          <span class="eyebrow">Generated record / preview</span>
          <button id="clear-context" class="demo-link-button" type="button">
            Clear local context
          </button>
        </div>
        <pre
          class="demo-json"
          id="write-preview"
          tabindex="0"
        >Start a run to generate synthetic agent records.</pre>
      </article>

      <article class="demo-panel">
        <div class="demo-panel-heading">
          <span class="eyebrow">02 / Reader</span>
          <span class="demo-terminal-label">STORAGE → GET</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Recall it from another context.</h2>
        <label for="record-index">
          Record index · <span id="read-range">load memories first</span>
        </label>
        <div class="demo-read-controls">
          <input
            id="record-index"
            type="number"
            value="0"
            min="0"
            max="0"
            disabled
          />
          <button id="random-record" class="button" type="button" disabled>
            Random
          </button>
          <button
            id="read-record"
            class="button button-primary"
            type="button"
            disabled
          >
            Recall →
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="demo-read-timing">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Browser round-trip</span>
            <strong id="read-browser-ms">
              — <small>ms</small>
            </strong>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Backend HTTP read</span>
            <strong id="read-backend-ms">
              — <small>ms</small>
            </strong>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="demo-result-heading">
          <span id="read-verification">Waiting for a stored record</span>
          <a
            id="reader-tab"
            href="/demo/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            hidden
          >
            Open reader in new tab ↗
          </a>
        </div>
        <pre
          class="demo-json demo-read-json"
          id="read-output"
          tabindex="0"
        >The reader fetches the value from instantKV.

No browser-local value cache.
No simulated storage.
No account needed.</pre>
        <p id="read-key" class="demo-record-key">
          Exact key and revision will appear here.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-instruments" aria-label="Measured write statistics">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Acknowledged</span>
        <strong id="metric-count">0</strong>
        <small>records stored</small>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Payload written</span>
        <strong id="metric-bytes">0</strong>
        <small>MiB · JSON values</small>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">End-to-end rate</span>
        <strong id="metric-rate">—</strong>
        <small>records / second</small>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Backend p50</span>
        <strong id="metric-p50">—</strong>
        <small>ms / record</small>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Backend p99</span>
        <strong id="metric-p99">—</strong>
        <small>ms / record</small>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Failed requests</span>
        <strong id="metric-errors">0</strong>
        <small>browser API requests</small>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-trace" aria-label="Measured write latency trace">
      <div class="demo-panel-heading">
        <span class="eyebrow">Browser batch round-trip / live trace</span>
        <span id="trace-summary">No measurements yet</span>
      </div>
      <svg
        viewBox="0 0 1000 120"
        role="img"
        aria-label="Latency of each acknowledged write batch, in milliseconds"
      >
        <path d="M0 30H1000 M0 60H1000 M0 90H1000" class="trace-rules" />
        <polyline id="latency-trace" points="" class="trace-line" />
      </svg>
      <p id="demo-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">
        Ready. Choose a workload and store your first memories.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-notes">
      <p>
        <strong>Real measurements, visible boundaries.</strong> Browser timings
        include Cloudflare, TLS, the network and the demo coordinator. Backend
        timings measure coordinator-to-Rust HTTP operations; they are not
        engine-only latency. Write percentiles combine acknowledged writes
        measured in this tab.
      </p>
      <p>
        Demo data expires after 15 minutes. RAM cache can be evicted under load
        and clears on restart. Durable mode commits through redb; its demo
        records also expire. This shared sandbox accepts synthetic context only.
        Managed hosting is still in development.
      </p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="text-link" href="/docs/live-demo/">
          Architecture & reproduce →
        </a>
        <a class="text-link" href="/benchmarks/">
          Controlled benchmarks →
        </a>
        <a class="text-link" href="/docs/quickstart/">
          Run your own node →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <noscript>
      <p>
        The interactive demo requires JavaScript. You can also run{' '}
        <code>instantkv demo --swarm</code> locally.
      </p>
    </noscript>
  </main>
  <script src="../scripts/demo.ts"></script>
</Base>
